course: dictionary
lesson: 683
title: Words that soothe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A balm is a thick, oily cream or ointment that soothes, heals or protects the skin. Read the clues in this sentence: «Cold wind and dry heating take water from the skin; licking your lips makes them more chapped, and lip balm helps.» Cold wind, dry heating and chapped lips are all problems, and lip balm helps with them. So a balm must be something that makes dry, sore skin feel better.
explain: Balm is a noun, and you can say a balm or balms. Lip balm is a balm for your lips. The word also has a second meaning: anything that comforts or calms you can be a balm. In «Music was a balm to her», the music made her feel calmer, so the word means comfort here, not cream.
explain: When you meet a word with two meanings, check the other words around it. Is the sentence about skin, or about feelings? If you swap in the meaning and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: A balm is a thick, oily cream or ointment.
fact: Lip balm stops lips cracking in cold or windy weather.
fact: Balms soothe dry skin, bites and small sores.
fact: Balm can also mean anything that comforts or calms you, as in «Music was a balm to her».
fact: Lemon balm is a herb, so the same word also names a plant.
exercise: What is a balm usually like? | A hard metal tool | *A thick, oily cream or ointment | A thin, watery drink | A loud, noisy song
exercise: «Licking your lips makes them more chapped.» What does chapped mean? | Covered in glitter | Warm and soft | *Dry and sore | Shiny and wet
exercise: Which thing could be a balm in the comfort sense? | A puddle in the road | *A kind word after a bad day | A ticket for the bus | A heavy wooden table
test: Why do people use lip balm in winter? | *It soothes lips and stops them cracking | It colours lips bright red | It makes lips grow bigger | It cools lips down with ice
test: Mum rubbed balm on the bee sting. What was the balm doing? | Making the sting bigger | Pulling the bee out | Hiding the sting from view | *Soothing the sting
exam: Tia said, «Hot chocolate was a balm after the snowy walk.» What does balm mean here? | *Something that comforts you | A cream for dry lips | A tool for cutting | A type of wet snow
